I think that the late game becomes relatively boring because there's
less that can cause you a big headache until the endgame.  In the
beginning, everything is dangerous, but once you're powerful enough,
killing mastodens is no tougher than killing newts.  The only things
that can kill you are enemies that use special attacks, like
cockatrices and mindflayers, and if they prove to be a pest they can be
quickly genocided.  Also YASDs, which will get you at any level, of
course!

So once you're past the Castle, the only thing that can be a threat is
Rodney, the Riders, and Demogorgon, if he shows up.  The other demons
are a laugh.

Not only do the monsters become less distinct later in the game, but
the nature of Gehennom gives way to boredom, which emphasises the need
to just hack and slash everything in the way so as to hurry up and find
the exits.

Oh, and I like the idea of customisable weapons.  I think that this
should be done as you level up.  For example, when you level up you get
a skill slot, but you could also get a weapon upgrade slot.  This would
give you an upgrade to the weapon of your choice (artifacts excluded?)
Perhaps the lightening addition mentioned would cost 2-3 slots, a stat
increase would cost one slot per stat up, and a creature-bane would
cost 1-2 slots.  So by explevel six, you'd have a spear that has a
lightening attack, does extra damage to (say) liches and increases your
charisma by one point.



